# Build output
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib
*.dll
!patch/minhook/lib/*.lib
!patch/detours/*.lib

# Visual Studio (patch/T7Patch/ is an intermediate dir VS creates beside the project)
.vs/
patch/T7Patch/
*.user

# JetBrains IDEs (Rider, etc.)
.idea/

# Local build/staging output
artifact/
packages/

# dev/build itself (the Docker-based local build script) and dev/README.md ARE tracked, so a
# Docker-based local build works out of the box for anyone on this branch. What stays excluded
# is dev/out/, the one directory a build writes to: every file in it (both DLLs and the injector
# exes) is produced from source in this repo on demand, so none of it belongs in git history.
dev/out/

# VS resource-editor binary, created once T7Patch.rc is opened in the designer
*.aps

# Local working notes — forensic findings from working on this codebase, deliberately
# never committed
NOTES.md

# Local AI-agent reference docs, not tracked upstream. AGENTS.md is the authoritative
# engineering reference for the C++ patch, generated from NOTES.md; CLAUDE.md is the working
# guide for Claude Code in this repo.
#
# Both are deliberately untracked. The consequence worth knowing: a fresh clone gets NEITHER, so
# anything a contributor genuinely must know to build or ship this project has to live in
# dev/README.md or injector/README.md instead - those two are the only tracked build docs.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# injector/ build output and fetched dependencies. The DLL payload under injector/assets/ is
# already covered by the *.dll rule above: it is produced by ./dev/build and embedded with
# include_bytes!, never committed.
injector/target/
injector/ui/node_modules/
# Vite output (`bun run build`), regenerated on every build.
injector/ui/dist/
# tauri-build regenerates these from capabilities/ and the plugin set on every build.
injector/src-tauri/gen/

# Parked implementation, kept on disk only. The .NET injector was never committed (it lived in
# the index alone), so it is moved here rather than deleted while the Tauri port takes over.
# Ignored so it can never be committed by accident, and so a `git add -A` after the switch does
# not resurrect it into the tree.
LeaveJustInCase/

# Claude Code's local state and any locally-installed agent skills. Nothing here is part of the
# project: it currently holds a 1205-line frontend-design skill that has no connection to a C++
# game patch, and `git add -A` would commit it. Whitelist a specific skill directory here if one
# is ever genuinely meant to be shared with contributors.
.claude/

# Upstream's local reverse-engineering inputs (stock game symbols). Upstream also ignored a
# root tools/ directory; that rule is dropped here because tools/ holds this repo's tracked
# offset lint. Keep any local RE tooling outside tools/.
stock-symbols/
